  "title": "fix round 1: B5 v6 T-1629 new failure tests lack task ids (KeyError 'id' in full suite)",
  "spec": "Fix round 1 for T-1629 (B5 v6, goal T-1403). Gate red 2026-10-03 15:12: the full suite errors in the two new tests in tests/test_failures.py, both with KeyError: 'id' raised from failures._rejecting_reviews (task[\"id\"]), reached from failure_kind (the gate_red assertion at the end of test_failure_kind_incomplete_for_execute_incomplete_holds) and from failure_signature (test_failure_signature_for_incomplete_uses_head_and_dirty_set). The task dicts built in those tests have no 'id'. In the focused run no review rows existed, so the list comprehension never indexed the task; in the full suite earlier tests leave review rows in the harness bus, so it does. The production code is correct: real tasks always have an id.\n\nChange (tests only): give every task dict built in these two tests an 'id' (a unique value no review row names, e.g. 'T-incomplete-<n>' / 'T-sig-<n>'), as the neighbouring tests in the same file do (grep '\"id\": \"T-' there). The id is not part of the signature, so equal-signature pairs may use different ids; keep every existing assertion. Do not change any module under orchestrator/.\n\nVerify: commit first. Then run tests/test_failures.py and tests/test_daemon.py in the foreground, then the whole tests directory once in the foreground with the same test command the gate hook uses (read .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh for it), to confirm the errors are gone under shared-bus ordering; report failures only. Never background a command. Branch: continue on task/T-1629 (head e1c4abc).",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1629"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_failures.py::test_failure_kind_incomplete_for_execute_incomplete_holds: passes: failure_kind returns 'incomplete' for hold_reason 'execute_incomplete: no commits' and for 'execute_incomplete: uncommitted changes' with an ordinary partial_output such as 'non-JSON output (rc=143): ' even when partial_output contains the word 'conflict'; returns 'quota' when partial_output contains 'usage limit reached', 'permissions' when it contains 'permission denied', 'environment' when it contains 'ModuleNotFoundError'; a hold with resume_hint missing returns 'incomplete'; existing kinds for gate_red and review holds are unchanged",
    "tests/test_failures.py::test_failure_signature_for_incomplete_uses_head_and_dirty_set: passes: for pipeline.failure_kind 'incomplete', failure_signature differs for two holds with different resume_hint.head or different dirty sets, is equal for identical ones regardless of dirty-path order, treats a missing head as empty, and the signature of a gate_red hold is unchanged from before this change for the same input",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_auto_fix_round_files_round_for_execute_incomplete_hold: passes: auto_fix_round files 'fix round 1' with fix_round_for the held id for a held task 'execute_incomplete: no commits' (pipeline.failure_kind 'incomplete', pipeline.auto_fix_route 'routine_incomplete'); a second pass files nothing; a hold whose partial_output carries a quota marker gets no round and no escalation notify; an identical second incomplete hold in the same lineage is escalated as repeated; with auto_fix_rounds 2 a third incomplete hold in the lineage gets no round; with [planner].autonomous True and routes enabled the incomplete round is still filed without calling decision.route; a task with status 'failed' and reason 'non-JSON output (rc=1): ' gets no round and no pipeline write",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_fix_round_note_fences_leftovers_and_guards_missing_worktree: passes: the round spec for an incomplete hold whose worktree exists contains a data fence with the hold_reason, the head, the worktree path and each recorded dirty path, and no diff hunk; a dirty path containing three backticks cannot close the fence; partial_output appears inside the failure-text fence; when the held worktree path does not exist the note reads 'worktree: missing', says the leftovers are not recoverable and does not name the path; a gate_red round renders an empty incomplete note"
  ],
